<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103882" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τητάομαι</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τᾱτ-</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τήτη</span>) 
			Pass.
		, only used in pres., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be in want</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺ δὲ τητᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					408
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τητᾶσθαι</span>
			<i>privation</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				265
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τητῶνται</span> shd. be read for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡττῶνται</span> (or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπατῶνται</span>) in <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.4.33
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> elsewh.
			always c. gen., <i>to be in want of, be deprived</i> or <i>bereft
				of</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίλων τατώμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					10.78
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				274
			</span></i>; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρός], πατρός,
			νυμφίων</span>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1618
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hec.</u>
				324
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἐμῶν τ. πρὸς τοῦ κακίστου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					383
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδέρκτων ὀμμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>OC</u>
					1200
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑλλάδος τητώμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Heracl.</u>
					31
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορῶν τ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>El.</u>
				310
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαρμάτων τητώμεθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1084
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥυθμοῦ τε καὶ ἁρμονίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					810b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐγενείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1099b2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔργου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					4.134c
				</span></i>
			.</div>
